Metric:
- id: itsm.case_resolution_time
- name: ITSM Case Resolution Time
- description: The ITSM Case Resolution Time metric measures the average duration taken to resolve IT service management cases from the moment they are logged until they are marked as resolved. This metric provides insights into the efficiency of the IT support team in addressing and resolving user issues, reflecting both the responsiveness and effectiveness of the service delivery process. It encompasses all types of service cases, including incidents, requests, and changes, ensuring a comprehensive view of support performance. By analyzing this metric, organizations can identify bottlenecks in their workflows, assess the adequacy of resources, and implement improvements to enhance service quality. Ultimately, this metric serves as a key performance indicator for IT service management, guiding strategic decisions to optimize support operations.

