- description: The ITSM Incident Reopen Rate measures the percentage of incidents that are reopened after they have been marked as resolved or closed. This metric serves as an indicator of the effectiveness and quality of the incident resolution process within IT Service Management workflows. A high reopen rate may suggest deficiencies in the initial diagnosis, inadequate solutions, or insufficient follow-up with users. It reflects the robustness of remediation efforts and the overall reliability of the IT support team in addressing issues. Monitoring this metric helps organizations identify areas for improvement in incident management practices and enhance user satisfaction.

