Metric:
- id: hr.onboarding_cycle_time
- name: HR Onboarding Cycle Time
- description: The HR Onboarding Cycle Time metric quantifies the duration required to complete the onboarding process for new employees, from the moment an offer is accepted to the point where the employee is fully integrated into the organization. This metric encompasses various stages of the onboarding workflow, including document submission, training completion, and IT provisioning, thereby reflecting the efficiency of HR processes and the effectiveness of cross-departmental collaboration. By measuring this cycle time, organizations can identify bottlenecks in their onboarding procedures, assess the responsiveness of IT services, and enhance overall employee experience. A shorter onboarding cycle time typically indicates streamlined workflows and effective resource allocation, while longer times may signal areas needing improvement. This metric is crucial for HR departments aiming to optimize their onboarding strategies and ensure timely integration of new hires into the workforce.

