- description: Backlog Aging measures the duration that unresolved items, such as tickets, requests, or feature enhancements, remain in the system without resolution. This metric provides insights into the age distribution of these items, allowing organizations to identify operational bottlenecks that may hinder workflow efficiency. By analyzing the aging of backlog items, teams can prioritize their efforts on older requests that may be impacting service levels or user satisfaction. The scope of this metric encompasses all unresolved items across various departments, including IT support, HR requests, and product development features. Understanding backlog aging helps organizations streamline processes and improve response times, ultimately enhancing overall service delivery.

