- description: Data Sync Latency measures the time delay between data synchronization events across various integrated systems within an enterprise architecture. This metric is crucial for assessing the efficiency and effectiveness of data flow between systems such as ERP, HR, and ITSM platforms. High latency values may indicate potential risks to data consistency, leading to discrepancies in reporting and decision-making processes. By monitoring this latency, organizations can identify bottlenecks in data transfer and take corrective actions to ensure timely updates. The scope of this metric encompasses all integrated systems that rely on real-time or near-real-time data synchronization to maintain operational integrity.

