Metric:
- id: mdm.duplicate_rate
- name: MDM Duplicate Rate
- description: The MDM Duplicate Rate measures the frequency of duplicate master data records present across various enterprise systems, such as ERP, HR, and ITSM platforms. This metric highlights the effectiveness of Master Data Management (MDM) governance by identifying quality gaps that may lead to inconsistencies in data reporting and decision-making. A high duplicate rate indicates potential issues in data entry processes, data integration, or data stewardship practices. By monitoring this rate, organizations can assess the health of their master data and implement necessary controls to enhance data quality. Ultimately, this metric serves as a critical indicator of the reliability and accuracy of foundational data used across business operations.

