- description: The Data Quality Exceptions Rate measures the frequency at which exceptions are raised by established data quality rules within an organization's ERP, HR, or ITSM systems. This metric focuses on identifying recurring issues related to data hygiene and governance, such as inaccuracies, inconsistencies, or missing information in critical datasets. By tracking these exceptions, organizations can pinpoint specific areas where data quality is lacking, enabling targeted interventions to improve overall data integrity. The scope of this metric encompasses all data inputs and outputs across relevant workflows, ensuring a comprehensive view of data quality challenges. Ultimately, this metric serves as a vital indicator of the effectiveness of data governance practices and the reliability of decision-making processes reliant on accurate data.

