- description: The Platform Customization Debt Index quantifies the extent of technical debt incurred through custom modifications made to an enterprise platform. This metric evaluates the cumulative impact of these customizations on the system's upgradeability, maintainability, and overall flexibility. It highlights potential risks associated with future upgrades, as excessive customization can complicate integration with new features or patches. By measuring this debt, organizations can better understand the trade-offs between immediate customization needs and long-term system health. Ultimately, this index serves as a critical indicator for decision-makers to assess the sustainability of their platform's architecture.

